I've compiled on the PC and posted my results before.  I'm in favor of
creating two versions for the pc, one for short time play and one for
long time play.  The short time version would be as small as possible, so
I can run it in a desqview window, and would have ease-of-use and neat things
defined. For instance, comand line completion, redo, tolkien if possible,
elbereth, wizard,etc.  I.e. something I can play while I'm downloading
and be entertained.  The long-play version should have the serious options:
ALTARS, THEOLOGY, STRONGHOLD, ENDGAME, POLYSELF (I won't accept it without
this) MEDUSA, HARD-SEDUCE, SPELLS (this could be in the short play if there's room).
The executable I'm running now requires 560K and can run ok in 590K of free ram.
I also have found ( by teleporting to the castle level which has about the most 
monsters tyou will see) that 560K is the biggest program (That is 560K free mem
needed to load from exemod) that can be run in 590K, and from what others have
said, 590K seems to be the max ram you can reasonably have free.  I offer my
free time to head a standards setting committee, or be part of one, to settle
on the defines for these two versions.  Please EMAIL me if you want to be part, and
one week from today I will post the names of those on the committee, and what
Ideas are being talked about. The one week delay is to let us have a chance to
check out the level 2 patch, and because I'm going on vacation for a week.
SO MAIL ME IF YOU WANT TO BE ON THE STANDARDS COMMITTEE FOR THE IBM PC.  The
more people, the more likely we will produce a good mix, and not just someone's
favorite options.
